{"title":"1969 IMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Generalization_and_Idea_for_a_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Generalization and Idea for a Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Remarks_(added_by_pf02,_July_2024)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Remarks (added by pf02, July 2024)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prove that for all real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/1/a71bbde9ff55f7d4098d3492165a9a792d778ab8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1, x_2, y_1, y_2, z_1, z_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"142\" height=\"13\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/9/ba9a1c871bca7fe9a9b2a3ae2aa87679d8b44e3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 &gt; 0, x_2 &gt; 0, x_1y_1 - z_1^2 &gt; 0, x_2y_2 - z_2^2 &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"341\" height=\"21\" />, the inequality\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/6/d064cd5e072e62dbbd229299796392c38859cd85.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{8}{(x_1 + x_2)(y_1 + y_2) - (z_1 + z_2)^2} \\leq \\frac{1}{x_1y_1 - z_1^2} + \\frac{1}{x_2y_2 - z_2^2}\\]\" width=\"440\" height=\"42\" />\nis satisfied. Give necessary and sufficient conditions for equality.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/0/aa033c5adcef40a4d6fcffed3a11b7da3416d957.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=x_1y_1 - z_1^2&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"146\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/8/b98412ee0cf49c2e52d061fdd98c0b4f8516d34e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=x_2y_2 - z_2^2&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"147\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>From AM-GM:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b133c8e95358be3556b93830381a33732dc8b336.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{AB} \\le \\frac{A+B}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"124\" height=\"39\" /> with equality at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/e/3be115227b05ea0768ff45f7217aaf3c195892aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=B$\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/f/8bf238e81932960fb3bef39f033a17427715ebe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4AB \\le (A+B)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/f/90fc9d499f9a9455f6d579e43dc85db32d0ac3f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{A+B} \\le \\frac{A+B}{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"135\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/2/7e23bc927ee9f3a89baf53eea4a9e08e64fb03c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8}{2(A+B)} \\le \\frac{A+B}{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"158\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/d/f1d811cf7af4563c1002d56f1e8d83cd98e09415.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8}{2(A+B)} \\le \\frac{1}{A}+\\frac{1}{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"162\" height=\"43\" /> [Equation 1]\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/9198db265d5addbbd3239ffb5793a68025c9e224.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_1 + x_2)(y_1 + y_2) - (z_1 + z_2)^2=x_1y_1+x_2y_2+x_1y_2+x_2y_1-z_1^2-2z_1z_2-z_2^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"609\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/e/c2ed0e9b2fbef359e94aa497b8de0beb6c8bc621.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_1 + x_2)(y_1 + y_2) - (z_1 + z_2)^2=(A+B)+x_1y_2+x_2y_1-2z_1z_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"506\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/d/a6dc63cdd2e66977c9363a9b40fc7e92dedc7223.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1y_1&gt;z_1^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/3/1334296867be0452139bc04a951b3cac2568baba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2y_2&gt;z_2^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"21\" />, and using the Rearrangement inequality\n</p><p>then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/1/d41bdfaf516de0795cad16f598dd173ac64fa7d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1y_1+x_2y_2-z_1z_1-z_2z_2 \\le x_1y_2+x_2y_1-z_1z_2-z_1z_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"423\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/4/8243055f1627e3882eec84aa9fbc79d7cdede38b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A+B) \\le  x_1y_2+x_2y_1-2z_1z_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"245\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/d/72d554c1c1d38930f2440908335386f9e18e7aee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(A+B) \\le x_1y_1+x_2y_2+x_1y_2+x_2y_1-z_1^2-2z_1z_2-z_2^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"444\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/9/b29ab64cd6fd671c4d9ad3db581549cbfac689ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(A+B) \\le (x_1 + x_2)(y_1 + y_2) - (z_1 + z_2)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"339\" height=\"21\" /> [Equation 2]\n</p><p>Therefore, we can can use [Equation 2] into [Equation 1] to get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/3/783a1e06907a2babb927a1f5647bebd1b0e086d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8}{(x_1 + x_2)(y_1 + y_2) - (z_1 + z_2)^2} \\le \\frac{1}{A}+\\frac{1}{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"328\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Then, from the values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/b/8ab308942c0b83dd36fcea5f2ffb73eecd712c89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8}{(x_1 + x_2)(y_1 + y_2) - (z_1 + z_2)^2} \\leq \\frac{1}{x_1y_1 - z_1^2} + \\frac{1}{x_2y_2 - z_2^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"445\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>With equality at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/f/bcf1a19f92d6861373d8d58d5f4f7b5d132c3052.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1y_1 - z_1^2=x_2y_2 - z_2^2&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"206\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/5/d652d2d87331a8e7e5efed68d62c095dbeec8ab2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1=x_2, y_1=y_2, z_1=z_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"191\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>~Tomas Diaz. orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Generalization_and_Idea_for_a_Solution\">Generalization and Idea for a Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Generalization and Idea for a Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This solution is actually more difficult but I added it here for fun to see the generalized case as follows:\n</p><p>Prove that for all real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/a/3ba88da26dd41c984d3645a009027b5bdda55f3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i, b_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/0/f00340aba36745c22e8873fefef2b76a9f89b8aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=1,2,...,n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"17\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/3/323daa7cf3320a850ae8a109ef686fc714f42b15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i &gt; 0, b_i &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/7/97788a3d5501f69f20138ab208010a6cc4bcc7a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\prod_{i=1}^{n-1}a_i-a_n^{n-1}&gt;0, \\prod_{i=1}^{n-1}b_i-b_n^{n-1}&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"275\" height=\"55\" /> the inequality\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/f/f7f71af0a5c53f17dc2a6348d8ffc73b1e10bd4d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2^n}{\\prod_{i=1}^{n-1}(a_i + b_i) - (a_n + b_n)^{n-1}} \\leq \\frac{1}{\\prod_{i=1}^{n-1}a_i-a_n^{n-1}} + \\frac{1}{\\prod_{i=1}^{n-1}b_i-b_n^{n-1}}\\]\" width=\"516\" height=\"44\" />is satisfied.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/9/3c99442f656558c56e24238d90daf2b7dabd449d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=\\prod_{i=1}^{n-1}a_i-a_n^{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"141\" height=\"55\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/813245a1285c90960ae94387aae2dc4a99921ee7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\prod_{i=1}^{n-1}b_i-b_n^{n-1}&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"133\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>From AM-GM:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b133c8e95358be3556b93830381a33732dc8b336.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{AB} \\le \\frac{A+B}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"124\" height=\"39\" /> with equality at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/e/3be115227b05ea0768ff45f7217aaf3c195892aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=B$\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/f/8bf238e81932960fb3bef39f033a17427715ebe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4AB \\le (A+B)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/f/90fc9d499f9a9455f6d579e43dc85db32d0ac3f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{A+B} \\le \\frac{A+B}{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"135\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/4/154f5926ac2f6082f849d09b1f891a8d75d1657c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2^n}{2^{n-2}(A+B)} \\le \\frac{A+B}{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"184\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/b/17b0f6393f8ab4d1f6788151668ded98cefcba33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2^n}{2^{n-2}(A+B)} \\le \\frac{1}{A}+\\frac{1}{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"188\" height=\"43\" /> [Equation 3]\n</p><p>Here's the difficult part where I'm skipping steps:\n</p><p>we prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/6/3e67ab2e471733a2aab7e2f7ee93db921f51d6ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{n-2}(A+B) \\le \\prod_{i=1}^{n-1}(a_i + b_i) - (a_n + b_n)^{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"336\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>and replace in [Equation 3] to get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/4/744704cfed0ae892f753cd9052ebc54bf1bd86c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2^n}{\\prod_{i=1}^{n-1}(a_i + b_i) - (a_n + b_n)^{n-1}} \\le \\frac{1}{A}+\\frac{1}{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"316\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p>and replace the values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/a/bbadc6f4f232fcd37f34fa330419756f0be63f3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2^n}{\\prod_{i=1}^{n-1}(a_i + b_i) - (a_n + b_n)^{n-1}} \\leq \\frac{1}{\\prod_{i=1}^{n-1}a_i-a_n^{n-1}} + \\frac{1}{\\prod_{i=1}^{n-1}b_i-b_n^{n-1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"522\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p>with equality at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/3/ad320b16c162d333c29047d667e290ac76e42f1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i=b_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"17\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/0/f00340aba36745c22e8873fefef2b76a9f89b8aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=1,2,...,n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Then set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/7/1977ed3a7d0e3b06bab30365f870b67ea5a8efe2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=3, a_1=x_1, a_2=y_1, a_3=z_1, b_1=x_2, b_2=y_2, b_3=z_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"437\" height=\"18\" /> and substitute in the generalized inequality to get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/b/8ab308942c0b83dd36fcea5f2ffb73eecd712c89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8}{(x_1 + x_2)(y_1 + y_2) - (z_1 + z_2)^2} \\leq \\frac{1}{x_1y_1 - z_1^2} + \\frac{1}{x_2y_2 - z_2^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"445\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>with equality at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/5/d652d2d87331a8e7e5efed68d62c095dbeec8ab2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1=x_2, y_1=y_2, z_1=z_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"191\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>~Tomas Diaz. orders@tomasdiaz.com\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Remarks_.28added_by_pf02.2C_July_2024.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Remarks_(added_by_pf02,_July_2024)\">Remarks (added by pf02, July 2024)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Remarks (added by pf02, July 2024)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>1. The solution given above is incorrect.  The error is in the\nincorrect usage of the Rearrangement inequality.  The conclusion\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/1/d41bdfaf516de0795cad16f598dd173ac64fa7d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1y_1+x_2y_2-z_1z_1-z_2z_2 \\le x_1y_2+x_2y_1-z_1z_2-z_1z_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"423\" height=\"17\" />\nis false.  For a counterexample take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/f/4efafe824ab49ab86b14f4d0f04435b53fcca788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 = y_1 = 2, x_2 = y_2 = 1, z_1 = z_2 = 0.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"305\" height=\"17\" />.  The left hand side equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/b/80b3fb7e3006cf1e3046dcacefbc876a2e3f2b26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 - 0.25 - 0.25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"120\" height=\"15\" />\nand the right hand side equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/d/fbd006accc648c35df7955217da2e4cb83cce099.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 - 0.25 - 0.25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"120\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>2. The generalization is reasonable but the idea for a solution\nis unacceptably vague (at one crucial step, the author says\n\"Here's the difficult part where I'm skipping steps\").  I don't\nbelieve this can be developed into a real proof, since it just\nfollows the idea of the Solution above, which is incorrect.\n</p><p>3. I will give a solution below, which uses calculus.  I believe\nit should be possible to find an \"elementary\" solution (i.e. a\nsolution based on elementary algebra and geometry) is possible.\n</p><p>4. Much later (June 2026) I saw an elementary solution on the\ninternet.  I give the link below, in the section Solution 3.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, remark that given the conditions of the problem, it follows\nthat <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/8/ce869739d22bda6955d0449efc8c03d87412f39f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_1 &gt; 0, y_2 &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"17\" />.  Also, we can assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/d/a4d21289374b49fbfaa9a1342382df14e78d07c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1 \\ge 0, z_2 \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"17\" />.\nIndeed, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/a/e1adcb7dda8c4427a55c11cd68db68cfb2828532.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1 &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/1/f31f6f0a92da28fc42881f84531bfdd2a774ec01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1 &lt; -z_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"15\" />.  It follows\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/1/8d1ce3579a8c46f272e1a557b2e93e99cdebd64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1 + z_2 &lt; -z_1 + z_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"148\" height=\"15\" />, so \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43b277ee6179a9d10b08f88ffe1f5ee7b95ea538.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{(x_1 + x_2)(y_1 + y_2) - (z_1 + z_2)^2} &lt; \\frac{1}{(x_1 + x_2)(y_1 + y_2) - (-z_1 + z_2)^2}\\]\" width=\"520\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>So, if we proved the inequality for positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/a/9ea31e5c5613f025b5be8aca425d318168491d89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> it is also true\nfor negative <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/a/9ea31e5c5613f025b5be8aca425d318168491d89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>Now consider the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> of three variables\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/9/da98ae528688ab77d9d4bdc65a474f0344cea9bd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[F(x, y, z) = \\frac{1}{xy - z^2}\\]\" width=\"158\" height=\"40\" />\ndefined on the domain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/7/44765fed896dea3d1fbaa43e31c448f2b1ae42b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y &gt; 0, z \\ge 0, z^2 &lt; xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"183\" height=\"20\" />.  For simplicity,\ndenote a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/b/31b1e1af4531148cbc079023f68c2b0102c4ee69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y, z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"61\" height=\"20\" /> in the domain by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.  The inequality in the\nproblem can be rewritten as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/f/e2f5abe987b048d8625a65ecb16ab6a61bab678c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[F \\left( \\frac{P_1 + P_2}{2} \\right) \\le \\frac{1}{2}[F(P_1) + F(P_2)]\\]\" width=\"270\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>This follows immediately from the inequality expressing the\nfact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/f/8ff3686ed4734f57a923e57a56329cd1dce3eadd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F(x, y, z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" /> is a convex function.  (In fact, it\nis equivalent to the convexity of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, but this is not needed\nfor our proof of the given inequality.)  Therefore, it is enough\nto prove that the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/f/8ff3686ed4734f57a923e57a56329cd1dce3eadd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F(x, y, z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" /> is convex.\n</p><p>We will prove that this function is convex.  In fact, we will\nprove that the function is strictly convex.  This will\nimply that equality holds only when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/6/e86e6f392a133ed9ee91ea333a289e0cc5b4c6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1 = P_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"17\" />, in other words,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/d/6bda7c68797532ba2243d628a8d0424ea3679cb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 = x_2, y_1 = y_2, z_1 = z_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"191\" height=\"13\" />, which will give us the\nnecessary and sufficient conditions for equality.\n</p><p>We use the theorem which says that a twice differentiable function\ndefined on a convex set is convex if and only if its Hessian is\npositive definite.  Furthermore, if the Hessian is strictly positive\ndefinite, then the function is strictly convex.\n</p><p>The Hessian of the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/f/8ff3686ed4734f57a923e57a56329cd1dce3eadd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F(x, y, z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" /> is the 3x3 matrix <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> formed\nby the second derivatives of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/0/140735c37aba1e9b36c293e704cc7469ee17b655.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\partial^2 F}{\\partial x^2} \\hspace{20pt} \\frac{\\partial^2 F}{\\partial x \\partial y} \\hspace{20pt} \\frac{\\partial^2 F}{\\partial x \\partial z} \\\\ \\\\ \\\\ \\frac{\\partial^2 F}{\\partial y \\partial x} \\hspace{20pt} \\frac{\\partial^2 F}{\\partial y^2} \\hspace{20pt} \\frac{\\partial^2 F}{\\partial y \\partial z} \\\\ \\\\ \\\\ \\frac{\\partial^2 F}{\\partial z \\partial x} \\hspace{20pt} \\frac{\\partial^2 F}{\\partial z \\partial y} \\hspace{20pt} \\frac{\\partial^2 F}{\\partial z^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"180\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is positive definite if for any 3x1 vector <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/a/a7a8f86754e4bb04dd61c01e1dad284c05f9a255.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v^t H v \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"19\" />.  (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/f/84f7b24532ac7ee1d9b8b199af7d0d69b721558f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v^t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"16\" /> is the transpose of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, a matrix which is 1x3.)\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is strictly positive definite if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/c/c3cb91b09eba6d20d5ed25b8cee588a3fa24c033.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v^t H v &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" /> unless <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/f/c5f490387b7f39e9fa8152ae483296730a1ecc54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Explicitly, we need to show that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc6d9a6172d35127b6cb37ea92192caf7029a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> are three numbers,\nthen\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/8/d68d897f5ec3215f70bfac08163fe75ef07ccd8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 \\frac{\\partial^2 F}{\\partial x^2} + ab \\frac{\\partial^2 F}{\\partial x \\partial y} + ac \\frac{\\partial^2 F}{\\partial x \\partial z} + ab \\frac{\\partial^2 F}{\\partial y \\partial x} + b^2 \\frac{\\partial^2 F}{\\partial y^2} + bc \\frac{\\partial^2 F}{\\partial y \\partial z} + ac \\frac{\\partial^2 F}{\\partial z \\partial x} + bc \\frac{\\partial^2 F}{\\partial z \\partial y} + c^2 \\frac{\\partial^2 F}{\\partial z^2} \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"739\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>and that the expression is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/5/9952432253dd3c764faa67299b1e31546f1d710c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 0$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> only when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/9/cc982894b8c7c4612608c6d2b4899b2e2486c7c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = b = c = 0$\" width=\"106\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Before embarking on the computations proving the inequality\nexpressing the positive definiteness of the Hessian of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />,\nlet us show that the domain of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is convex.  Let\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/8/a18402f80743537dcb887f9512a57f9255d94775.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1 = (x_1, y_1, z_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"126\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/d/d0d313421e6dfeef28ff22779b7f71da4f03b936.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_2 = (x_2, y_2, z_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"126\" height=\"20\" /> be two\npoints in the domain of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.  This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/9/df9ceb8beb4637d59de1762078585c7d6be9fac6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1, y_1, x_2, y_2 &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"128\" height=\"17\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/3/9738b67a7732a77808dc37b568f5420985930e54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1, z_2 \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/4/6b499a675bd8b883ea8ed6ad6232199b3c274684.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1^2 &lt; x_1 y_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/8/c581f483e80d8263634bd92043c535b07c374b0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_2^2 &lt; x_2 y_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"21\" />.  We need\nto verify that the same is true for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/f/1fff9cb935eeaa9cbf6084f59d48251b547dd630.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = t P_1 + (1 - t) P_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"159\" height=\"20\" /> when\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/4/a0488ee735a04ceaf2e0e707425343131eed5c97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; t &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"15\" />.  The only thing which is not obvious is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/f/7ff10e4441359896a498659662a018c9d5300dc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[t z_1 + (1 - t) z_2]^2 &lt; [t x_1 + (1 - t) x_2] [t y_1 + (1 - t) y_2]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"406\" height=\"21\" />.\nTo see this, work out the multiplications, use what we already know about\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/c/3bcb9c64e387d0361db730a6500cc9271ed1e7de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"19\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/e/d1eabcb380f9897d7b74d17118a88bd9863b6dbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_2^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"19\" height=\"21\" />, simplify by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/c/02c190e2baea6797fd99ebc819c74ad843b26371.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t(1-t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" /> and we are left with showing\nthat <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c52ebe4e34c39eb1efbddb62b86513167d3dfab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 z_1 z_2 &lt; x_1 y_2 + x_2 y_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"17\" />.  This can be seen as follows:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/8/9885cf472cee312e1710cd9531ecc8a556a25a12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 z_1 z_2 &lt; 2 \\sqrt{x_1 y_1} \\sqrt{x_2 y_2} = 2 \\sqrt{(x_1 y_2) (x_2 y_1)} \\le x_1 y_2 + x_2 y_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"437\" height=\"35\" />.\n</p><p>Now work towards proving the inequality expressing that the Hessian\nof <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is positive definite.  Compute all the second derivatives of\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />; notice that they all have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/c/04cc2ad213e0d8e72700c290a504bc9df6b88a05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(xy - z^2)^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"21\" /> at the denominator, so\nwe can simplify with this factor.  (The computation is made somewhat\nshorter by taking advantage of the fact that the order of taking the\nderivatives makes no difference in mixed derivatives (for example \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/b/0db69caf8e1ee6664e5809d13442d505da9c0da2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\partial^2 F}{\\partial x \\partial y} = \\frac{\\partial^2 F}{\\partial y \\partial x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"117\" height=\"44\" />).)\n</p><p>We get (as the thing we have to prove) that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/5/215bff5e81d59e12065c1d26e1c500d38ea297b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a^2y^2 + 2ab(xy + z^2) - 8acyz + 2b^2x^2 - 8bcxz + c^2(2xy + 6z^2) \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"527\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/f/7dfc9e7d175fffb21a59d686cccbe222a384b4c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = b = 0$\" width=\"74\" height=\"12\" /> the expression equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/4/db496a2fade0867e2dedc83ca9cf6262560559a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> as well.\nSo, assume that at least one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/3/3834f0cef2a1f4d8524aa5bc8e3faca298550862.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/4/f6450fe20e3a83ab6792c53c485674a2b69edf4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ne 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />.  We can assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/3/b93542ba7ddfa6e5d5aa9ec642446b0c8fea7efc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\ne 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" />.\nWe will show that in this case, the expression is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/9/1b98a367e7a3b900016ce23ba8ecaa33ce029c6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Simplify by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and rearrange the terms so we can think of the expression\non the left as a polynomial in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2c177987014bafc8bc176b7dbfde6a28855c475.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(xy + 3z^2)c^2 - 4(xb + ya)zc + [x^2b^2 + y^2a^2 + (xy + z^2)ab] &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"489\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Notice that this is a polynomial (in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />) of degree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of the type\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/2/152ce0cd3383f8dbbe92cd362af22e015269857a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AX^2 + BX + C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"129\" height=\"18\" />, whose leading coefficient is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/9/1b98a367e7a3b900016ce23ba8ecaa33ce029c6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />.  To show that its\nvalues are always <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/9/1b98a367e7a3b900016ce23ba8ecaa33ce029c6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> we need to show that its discriminant is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a31e002bb10fa9452564aacac90861fa688882ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" />,\nin other words, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/e/1bef85c710dd6122a2bbaabaacddaa2c5a9441e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B^2 - 4AC &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, we need to show that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/c/a2c1c3d256ee48700e8d56c2fcf9210ccae3f071.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16[(xb + ya)z]^2 - 4(xy + 3z^2)[x^2b^2 + y^2a^2 + (xy + 3z^2)ab] &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"489\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>After factoring out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and working out all multiplications, this becomes\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/1/6b1a7ac8fb7efb7f9d11ba2f6a49201dac8ebed6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-x^3yb^2 + x^2z^2b^2 - xy^3a^2 + y^2z^2a^2 - x^2y^2ab + 4xyz^2ab - 3z^4ab &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"529\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>After some rearranging of terms, grouping, and factoring, this becomes\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/e/07e310640089f81dbf0e51a2b986f53a65464e2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-(xy - z^2)[x^2b^2 + (xy - 3z^2)ab + y^2a^2] &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"344\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/a/b0a796b98e29670f57d0a583284bb8cda38a1cb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 &lt; xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"20\" />, we need to show\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/f/f4f52a0e3846228b128f1f64d5439f9afdea868d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2b^2 + (xy - 3z^2)ab + y^2a^2 &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"246\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Now, view the expression on the left hand side as a polynomial of degree\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, whose leading coefficient is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/9/1b98a367e7a3b900016ce23ba8ecaa33ce029c6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />.  To conclude that its\nvalues are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/9/1b98a367e7a3b900016ce23ba8ecaa33ce029c6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> we need to show that its discriminant is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a31e002bb10fa9452564aacac90861fa688882ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" />.  That\nis, we need to show that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/1/8f12536e01cc5562ef8aa2b11a0c500d9c54f366.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[(xy - 3z^2)a]^2 - 4x^2y^2a^2 &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"228\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Work out the multiplications, and regroup terms to get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/c/d0c4228dc641568987151a451bab5ffd9d8241de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3a^2(xy - z^2)(xy + 3z^2) &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"231\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>This is clearly true, which concludes the proof.\n</p><p>[Solution by pf02, July 2024]\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>See <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://prase.cz/kalva/imo/isoln/isoln696.html\">https://prase.cz/kalva/imo/isoln/isoln696.html</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let us define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/3/ed3d6fd16803ce6628ee0df7346730f5e1119b43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x, y, z) = \\frac{1}{xy-z^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"159\" height=\"42\" />. Then, the problem states\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/e/d6eed9f99ef37612adfdb3db34fe5dd7a3abf78d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2f\\left(\\frac{x_1+x_2}{2}, \\frac{y_1+y_2}{2}, \\frac{z_1+z_2}{2}\\right) \\le f(x_1,y_1,z_1)+f(x_2,y_2,z_2),\\]\" width=\"476\" height=\"43\" />\nthat is, that the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is convex on the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/7/8779a4d2bb97525ce64b069644599209e25986b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D = \\{(x,y,z)\\in\\mathbb{R}^2|xy-z^2&gt;0\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"259\" height=\"21\" />. It is known that a twice continuously differentiable function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/6/546fa8f0e132189a3bfbc1ab4dbf6ecfdd6fa3d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(t_1,t_2,\\dots,t_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"20\" /> is convex if its Hessian <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/f/f5f7f3597a1d53dc7975cefc1a2cf9d605e456ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[f&#39;&#39;_{ij}]_{i,j=1}^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"65\" height=\"23\" /> is positive definite, or equivalently (by Sylvester's criterion), if its principal minors<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/d/bbd2f2a568d6ae2a3318f67d47e5be7559a65c64.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[D_k=\\det[f&#39;&#39;_{ij}]_{i,j=1}^k, k=1,\\dots,n\\]\" width=\"238\" height=\"22\" />are positive. In the case of our <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/c/dfc896474709e1d0a6d3f4763e6bae17c2453456.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[D_1=\\frac{2y^2}{(xy-z^2)^3}, D_2=3xy+\\frac{z^2}{(xy-z^2)^5}, D_3=\\frac{6}{(xy-z^2)^6},\\]\" width=\"464\" height=\"44\" />\nwhich are all obviously positive. Thus, we are done.\n</p><p><br />\n<i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO\" title=\"1969 IMO\">1969 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1969 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1969 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1969 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1969 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1969 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1969 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1969_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1969 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017170130\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.060 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.076 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 771/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1211/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 51/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 29887/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.159      1 -total\n 53.01%    6.445      1 Template:IMO_box\n 45.98%    5.591      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15718:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017170130 and revision id 288540. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}